  │     File     │                                 Responsibility                                 │   Depends on    │
  ├──────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mrules.js[39m     │ Rule factories: [38;5;153mrequired[39m, [38;5;153mminLength[39m, [38;5;153mmaxLength[39m, [38;5;153mpattern[39m, [38;5;153memail[39m, [38;5;153mmatches[39m        │ nothing         │
  ├──────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mvalidate.js[39m  │ [38;5;153mvalidate(values, schema)[39m → [38;5;153m{ valid, errors }[39m                                   │ nothing         │
  ├──────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mbind-form.js[39m │ [38;5;153mbindForm(formEl, schema, onValid, options)[39m — reads inputs, renders errors,     │ DOM,            │
  │              │ calls back                                                                     │ [38;5;153mvalidate.js[39m     │
  ├──────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mindex.js[39m     │ Re-exports the public surface                                                  │ the other three │
  └──────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────┘

  The pure/DOM split is what makes the rules testable in plain Node with no browser harness; [38;5;153mbind-form.js[39m is the only
  file that touches the document. Consumers import from [38;5;153msrc/validation/index.js[39m and never reach into the internals, so
  the rule implementations stay free to change.

  [1mChanged:[0m
  - [38;5;153mapp.js[39m — [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m is deleted; the login schema and a [38;5;153mbindForm[39m call replace both it and the hand-written submit
    handler. [38;5;153mlogin()[39m stays as-is, called from the [38;5;153monValid[39m callback.
  - [38;5;153mindex.html[39m — [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m, plus an error container per field and one for form-level errors.
  - [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m, [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m — converted CommonJS → ESM (4 lines of change total) so the whole repo is one module
    system.
  - [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m — add [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m.
  - [38;5;153mREADME.md[39m — note that the page must now be served over HTTP, with the one-line command to do it.

  [1mTwo consequences I want explicit before you say yes[0m, since they're the kind that bite later:

  1. Deleting [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m changes nothing observable — it's only called from the handler I'm replacing — but it is a
     working function being removed, so I'm naming it rather than burying it in a diff.
  2. [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m is repo-wide. [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m are the only other JS here and they convert cleanly,
     but any future [38;5;153m.js[39m file in this repo is an ES module by default from then on.

